Since `Guild.premium` is an optional 1-1 relation (docs: `orm/v6/prisma-schema/data-model/relations/index.mdx` §"Relations in Prisma Client", and `orm/v7/.../one-to-one-relations.mdx`), you update the nested `PremiumModel` through `prisma.guild.update` using `update` (must already exist) or `upsert` (create-or-update):

```ts
await prisma.guild.update({
  where: { guildId },
  data: {
    premium: {
      upsert: {
        create: { active: true, expiry, subtype_monthly: true },
        update: { active: true, expiry, subtype_monthly: true },
      },
    },
  },
});
```

Use `update: { ... }` instead of `upsert` if you're sure a `PremiumModel` row already exists for that guild (nested `update`/`connect`/`upsert` are the documented ops for 1-1 relations, per `prisma-client-reference.mdx` line ~5199-5201).

